{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310661,"nonce":"yCmHLMfInCceZNi2nn+kbpeIkuw=","title":"FIXED f4ac2514 (546-\u003e560): Null\u003cInt64\u003e = Int box with i64 payload; the ENTRY FILE IS COMPILED TWICE (import of itself) so statics got two ...","message":"Batch after 2a6bcc2d. git-bug c40a78a (closed), dfdaa34 (closed: doParse compiles), 91fda9b (open: duplicate compile), bd928b8 (open: Xml.parse throws, uncaught object prints as pointer).\n\n- **Null\u003cInt64\u003e box**: `optional_inner_is_boxable_primitive` is THE predicate for Optional\u003cscalar\u003e; Int64 boxes via `haxe_box_int_ptr(I64)`, unboxes `haxe_unbox_int_ptr -\u003e I64` only when the value is an optional scalar or in `boxed_value_regs`. Field reads of `.high/.low` on an Optional\u003cInt64\u003e receiver unbox first (`int64_word_read`). Ternary/null-eq classifier knows `Prim::Int64`.\n- **Entry file compiled twice**: the injected `new TestX()` resolves the entry file on the class path and compiles it as an import BEFORE the entry compile. Every class exists twice; a static had two globals. Skipping the import copy LOST 16 rows — the import copy supplies sibling-type declarations the entry compile lacks. Fix = alias: `metadata.rs` maps a static whose `Class.field` is in `external_globals` to that gid; reads/stores go through `static_global_for(symbol)` (qualified name) BEFORE the this-field fallback; `global_type_of(gid)` via `external_global_types`.\n- **Upstream Int64.hx** uses `abstract` as `this` (`Int64Helper.toFloat(abstract)`) — both parsers now accept `KwAbstract` in primary position.\n- `var a:Int64` resolves to the CLASS `___Int64`, so `a / b` took the float path — `int64_div` in operators.rs widens the other side to I64.\n- `Int32 * 4294967296.` typed Int32 — `over_int(ty)` abstract chain + Float side → Float in infer.rs; `operator_method_accepts` rejects Float actual for an Int formal.\n- Harness: `run.sh` scanned `function test*` at ANY brace depth, injecting calls to LOCAL functions (TestInt64.testCapture). Now depth-1 only; scored/skip unchanged 1100/140.\n- `bind_skipped_optional_args` filled TRAILING defaults with unbound sibling symbols (`fChain(2,3)` → `2,3,10`); now only real skips, through `lower_param_default` (binds param symbols + SymbolId(0)=this).\n- E0801 tag switch carried SIMD arms (`escapes.get` in haxe.xml.Parser) → Cranelift refused the whole function (`uses_wide_vectors`). Vector-receiver rows filtered (`takes_vector`). XML tests now RUN but throw — MOVED rows Issue11883/4094/4096 CRASH→COMPILE_FAIL(exit 1) are that.\n\n**How to apply:** when a static reads 0 that was written, ask whether the class was compiled twice (`RAYZOR_IMPORT_GRAPH=1`). Don't dedup the compile; alias the global. A MOVED row CRASH→exit 1 with `Uncaught exception: \u003cnumber\u003e` is a thrown OBJECT printed as its address.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_null_int64_box_and_entry_file_double_compile` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}